  "known_limits": [
    "These files are layered artwork, not a completed Cubism or Inochi model; no .moc3/.cmo3/.inp is claimed by this artwork delivery.",
    "Static endpoint assemblies were reviewed at 320px display and 640px Retina scale. Native mesh interpolation, blink transitions, audio lip-sync, opacity switching and motion physics still require actual renderer QA.",
    "Head/face motion is supported only at reviewed modest frontal ranges: gaze +/-3 source pixels, head translation example +6/-4 source pixels, forearm example +/-4 degrees. Large turns, profile anatomy and wide arm excursions are not completed.",
    "Front hair and headdress are a combined visible layer; eyebrows remain embedded in that artwork. Do not claim independent eyebrow/bangs control.",
    "Torso, apron, skirt and legs use a foreground/body-underpaint group; independent shoe/leg choreography is not supplied.",
    "Independent tail motion remains blocked in the frozen core. A separate tail-underpaint experiment exists but is not accepted for release.",
    "RiceHoldingArmBowl combines the left sleeve, supporting hand and bowl in one component; the pose is coherent but is not independent bowl-front/rice-back anatomical separation. Right spoon arm and removable rice bite are separate.",
    "When rice arms show, core idle ForearmHandL/R must be hidden exclusively. Core UpperArms and RiceElbowBridge pieces preserve elbow overlap. Avoid simultaneous idle/rice limb cross-fades that show four hands.",
    "Mood preview eye narrowing is a composited endpoint guide. Native partial eyelids and iris behavior must be inspected rather than assuming static endpoint transforms prove realistic intermediate blinking.",
    "Sleepy expression is separate from the actual sleep lock; full sleep must show closed-eye assets and suppress eating and audio/input mouth responses.",
    "Some source-scale one-pixel fringe/temple/contact-edge artifacts remain but were not visibly disruptive in the accepted 320px proofs. Follow actual renderer findings rather than restarting static perfection loops.",
    "Production v3 uses authorized generated fill and registered redraw, so the old stage1 zero-pixel-difference claim does not apply to v3."
  ],
